feat(candidates): probability-sorted strip with cutoff; deepening off by default

- llama.ts: parseTopTokens now returns {token, prob} sorted descending
  (handles prob and logprob fields); mergeCandidates merges duplicate
  words by summing probabilities and re-sorts.
- controller.ts: tokens below the probability cutoff (setting, default
  1%) are dropped before any completion request is spent; Candidate
  carries prob end to end. Default maxDepth is now 1 = idle deepening
  disabled until the single-word flow is tuned.
- strip.ts/styles.css: candidates render vertically, one per line, with
  the probability in brackets, e.g. "France (36%)"; sub-1% shows (<1%).
- settings.ts: new "Probability cutoff" slider; Max depth documents
  that 1 disables deepening.
- tests: unit suite updated for weighted candidates (25 cases), plus
  opt-in live integration tests (tests/llama-live.test.ts) that hit a
  real llama-server when LLAMA_ENDPOINT is set and log actual top
  tokens/completions for debugging model output.

Live test against localhost:8081 shows the Korean-garbage issue is the
model, not the plugin: gemma-4-26B-A4B-it (an instruct tune) puts 36%
on Korean tokens for an English prompt. A base model is required.
